[
    {
        "content": "<p>For various morphisms and they're respective <code>Equiv</code> variants, we have <code>FooEquiv.ofFooHom</code> which takes to morphisms and proofs that their compositions (as morphisms) are the identity and produces the <code>Equiv</code> variant. For example, see <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=RingEquiv.ofRingHom#doc\">docs#RingEquiv.ofRingHom</a>. For these, we can / do / sometimes have one or more of the following lemmas marked as <code>simp</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooEquiv</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ofFooHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">FooEquiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FooHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ofFooHom_apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ofFooHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">coe_ofFooHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⇑</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ofFooHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ofFooHom_symm_apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ofFooHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">symm_ofFooHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ofFooHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ofFooHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This causes some <code>simp</code> non-confluence because then <code>FooEquiv.symm_apply_apply</code> and <code>FooEquiv.apply_symm_apply</code> won't fire since the previous lemmas get applied first.</p>\n<p>My thought is that <code>_apply</code> and <code>_symm_apply</code> should not be marked <code>@[simp]</code> at all, and that <code>coe_</code> and <code>symm_</code> should be marked <code>@[simp low]</code>. What do others think here?</p>",
        "id": 608838054,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1783458962
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't think you can have both <code>coe_ofFooHom</code> and <code>ofFooHom_apply</code> be simp (don't think it would lint). Same with <code>ofFooHom_symm_apply</code> and <code>symm_ofFooHom</code>.</p>",
        "id": 608839512,
        "sender_full_name": "Monica Omar",
        "timestamp": 1783459606
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm pretty sure you <em>can</em> (and Mathlib has even had things like this) because the discr tree key for the <code>apply</code> versions is longer, and hence gets used first by <code>simp</code>, so there are no complaints from the <code>simpNF</code> linter.</p>",
        "id": 608839816,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1783459740
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In that case, yeah, I agree, we shouldn't have all of them simp, and <code>coe_</code> and <code>symm_</code> should be <code>@[simp low]</code> like you said.</p>\n<p>(personally, I don't see the reason of having <code>_apply</code> and <code>_symm_apply</code> if you already have <code>coe_</code> and <code>symm_</code>)</p>",
        "id": 608840194,
        "sender_full_name": "Monica Omar",
        "timestamp": 1783459877
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I feel like we have reached a consensus. Do we want to ask some more people to weight in? Or can we start applying these suggested changes to e.g. <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40841\">#40841</a>?</p>",
        "id": 612542070,
        "sender_full_name": "Tjeerd Jan Heeringa",
        "timestamp": 1784887487
    }
]